1
00:00:58,559 --> 00:00:59,393
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION

2
00:00:59,477 --> 00:01:00,978
CHILD ACTORS WERE FILMED SAFELY
WITH SUPERVISION

3
00:01:02,021 --> 00:01:03,189
What? Huh?

4
00:01:03,272 --> 00:01:04,482
Hit me, then!

5
00:01:04,565 --> 00:01:06,525
We have a crowd already.
Hit me! Come on!

6
00:01:07,818 --> 00:01:11,071
Ms. Choi and Mr. Kang
were not together that day.

7
00:01:12,490 --> 00:01:14,283
How could you possibly know that?

8
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:16,869
Because I was the one
who was with Mr. Kang.

9
00:01:16,952 --> 00:01:18,037
What?

10
00:01:27,171 --> 00:01:28,297
Mr. Kang and I

11
00:01:29,465 --> 00:01:30,633
are dating.

12
00:01:39,558 --> 00:01:43,145
I believed I was the only one
who could clear Mr. Kang’s name.

13
00:01:43,896 --> 00:01:45,397
Is this your answer

14
00:01:46,232 --> 00:01:47,316
to my marriage proposal?

15
00:01:50,569 --> 00:01:51,529
Yes.

16
00:01:54,240 --> 00:01:55,449
I believed my courage

17
00:01:56,158 --> 00:01:58,994
was the only thing that could protect us.

18
00:02:00,454 --> 00:02:01,372
However…

19
00:02:03,457 --> 00:02:05,459
that was nothing but arrogance.

20
00:02:05,543 --> 00:02:06,961
When did you start dating?

21
00:02:07,753 --> 00:02:09,088
Who made the first move?

22
00:02:09,171 --> 00:02:10,130
Are you really getting married?

23
00:02:14,426 --> 00:02:15,511
Well, actually…

24
00:02:15,594 --> 00:02:16,470
Oh, no.

25
00:02:16,554 --> 00:02:18,138
-Ms. Cha.
-Ms. Choi.

26
00:02:18,222 --> 00:02:19,473
A word, please.

27
00:02:27,356 --> 00:02:29,316
Is Ms. Cha about to get her hair torn out?

28
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:32,111
Are you kidding?
She should be the one pulling.

29
00:02:33,279 --> 00:02:34,613
In any case, it's super entertaining.

30
00:02:39,368 --> 00:02:40,703
Why did you do that?

31
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:42,913
I couldn't stand

32
00:02:42,997 --> 00:02:46,917
listening to people drag your names
through the mud like that.

33
00:02:49,461 --> 00:02:52,298
Did you not expect
they'd drag you into the mud too?

34
00:02:53,382 --> 00:02:55,718
But us dating is the truth,

35
00:02:56,302 --> 00:02:58,012
so at least I won't feel wronged.

36
00:02:58,596 --> 00:02:59,597
You're just…

37
00:03:07,021 --> 00:03:10,316
Just how much more are you trying
to make me feel indebted to you?

38
00:03:11,317 --> 00:03:12,234
Don't say that.

39
00:03:14,236 --> 00:03:16,822
You have no idea
what kind of awful thoughts I had.

40
00:03:21,911 --> 00:03:23,704
People are more cruel

41
00:03:23,787 --> 00:03:26,081
than you'd think. It'll be very tough.

42
00:03:27,458 --> 00:03:28,292
I know.

43
00:03:28,584 --> 00:03:29,877
But don't let them break you.

44
00:03:31,045 --> 00:03:32,004
Ever.

45
00:03:33,714 --> 00:03:34,840
I won't, Ms. Choi.

46
00:03:46,602 --> 00:03:48,604
It was such a long day.

47
00:03:51,482 --> 00:03:53,275
So then, when are we getting married?

48
00:03:53,359 --> 00:03:54,985
Quit teasing!

49
00:03:55,069 --> 00:03:57,696
People are already
pestering me about it as it is.

50
00:03:58,447 --> 00:04:00,115
Why'd you have to bring up the proposal?

51
00:04:02,868 --> 00:04:04,745
We should say we're dating
with marriage in mind

52
00:04:04,828 --> 00:04:06,497
to avoid any unnecessary drama.

53
00:04:08,624 --> 00:04:09,833
I guess you're right.

54
00:04:10,709 --> 00:04:13,379
People really do love to gossip.

55
00:04:15,589 --> 00:04:16,507
Thank you

56
00:04:17,675 --> 00:04:19,259
for bravely stepping up.

57
00:04:21,303 --> 00:04:23,806
My reputation's cleared thanks to you.

58
00:04:25,307 --> 00:04:26,141
I'm glad.

59
00:04:27,184 --> 00:04:30,104
I was worried
I'd intervened unnecessarily.

60
00:04:33,273 --> 00:04:34,191
Well, then.

61
00:04:35,067 --> 00:04:36,485
Shall we shop for wedding dresses?

62
00:04:37,695 --> 00:04:38,529
Stop it.

63
00:04:43,909 --> 00:04:45,577
We have to book a venue first.

64
00:04:49,123 --> 00:04:50,749
You should brace yourself.

65
00:04:51,375 --> 00:04:54,461
Even the copy machines
and water coolers will pester you today.

66
00:04:56,255 --> 00:04:57,923
Should I just call in sick and go home?

67
00:04:58,007 --> 00:04:59,925
Then people will say you quit.

68
00:05:01,427 --> 00:05:02,261
I can't let that happen.

69
00:05:05,431 --> 00:05:06,265
Ms. Cha.

70
00:05:09,268 --> 00:05:12,563
Look, I think I misspoke yesterday.

71
00:05:12,646 --> 00:05:14,606
I hope you didn't take it the wrong way.

72
00:05:14,690 --> 00:05:17,568
All I meant was
no matter how hard one works,

73
00:05:17,651 --> 00:05:19,695
they still need to get sleep.

74
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:21,321
Something like that.

75
00:05:22,823 --> 00:05:23,866
Yeah, okay.

76
00:05:23,949 --> 00:05:26,118
Why would someone post
something like that?

77
00:05:27,453 --> 00:05:29,038
By the way, are you okay making

78
00:05:29,747 --> 00:05:31,123
your relationship public?

79
00:05:33,167 --> 00:05:35,335
-People will see!
-One kiss before someone comes.

80
00:05:37,546 --> 00:05:39,923
It's better than sneaking around
and getting caught.

81
00:05:40,549 --> 00:05:41,383
Sorry?

82
00:05:51,143 --> 00:05:52,936
Oh my, congratulations on getting married.

83
00:05:53,020 --> 00:05:55,230
No, we're not doing it immediately.

84
00:05:55,981 --> 00:05:57,566
Hey, look! It's Mr. Kang.

85
00:05:58,484 --> 00:06:00,652
Wow, do we finally
get to see you in the same shot?

86
00:06:06,575 --> 00:06:07,951
Doors are closing.

87
00:06:20,255 --> 00:06:21,799
EPISODE 11

88
00:06:21,882 --> 00:06:24,927
EVEN IF RUMORS BLUR THE TRUTH,
STILL CLOCKING IN!

89
00:06:26,804 --> 00:06:29,223
Do I have to
keep giving you this in secret?

90
00:06:29,807 --> 00:06:31,725
I was just caught off guard earlier.

91
00:06:31,809 --> 00:06:32,684
Wait, what?

92
00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:38,398
So all this time,
it was Mr. Kang that has been

93
00:06:38,482 --> 00:06:40,109
putting tea on Ms. Cha's desk?

94
00:06:40,192 --> 00:06:41,360
Yes.

95
00:06:42,653 --> 00:06:43,821
Unbelievable!

96
00:06:43,904 --> 00:06:46,532
I had no clue you two were dating.

97
00:06:46,615 --> 00:06:48,158
You could've given me a heads-up.

98
00:06:49,034 --> 00:06:51,120
Mr. Kang, what about my tea?

99
00:06:51,203 --> 00:06:53,330
You can make your own, Mr. Jeon.

100
00:06:53,413 --> 00:06:54,790
Unbelievable.

101
00:06:54,873 --> 00:06:56,834
You used to make it for me yourself.

102
00:06:56,917 --> 00:06:58,001
You've changed.

103
00:06:58,752 --> 00:07:01,672
How about our outside meeting?
Do you want to go separately?

104
00:07:04,091 --> 00:07:05,008
The outside meeting…

105
00:07:05,092 --> 00:07:07,719
Should I go, since it's a project
I was working on with Ms. Cha?

106
00:07:07,803 --> 00:07:08,679
No.

107
00:07:08,762 --> 00:07:11,807
We're getting a response to our proposal,
so I need to be there myself.

108
00:07:12,391 --> 00:07:13,684
Then should I go with Mr. Kang?

109
00:07:13,767 --> 00:07:16,436
No, I wrote that proposal,
so I should be the one to go.

110
00:07:16,520 --> 00:07:17,354
Sure.

111
00:07:18,730 --> 00:07:20,899
Then let's head out together
when it's time.

112
00:07:27,030 --> 00:07:30,033
I'm a little hurt I was left in the dark,

113
00:07:30,117 --> 00:07:31,910
but you two make a great couple.

114
00:07:33,912 --> 00:07:36,081
You're so damn out of touch.
How did you not notice it?

115
00:07:36,165 --> 00:07:37,541
-You knew?
-Of course, I did.

116
00:07:37,624 --> 00:07:39,626
One look, and I know.

117
00:07:39,710 --> 00:07:41,837
-I was the only one who didn't know?
-Exactly!

118
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:43,505
Oh, man.

119
00:07:44,381 --> 00:07:45,215
Yeah, what's up?

120
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:48,051
Oh, tonight?

121
00:07:48,135 --> 00:07:49,178
Sounds good.

122
00:07:49,261 --> 00:07:50,721
Sure, I'll let Ji-yoon know and--

123
00:07:50,804 --> 00:07:51,930
No, that'll be too awkward.

124
00:07:52,598 --> 00:07:53,432
What?

125
00:07:53,515 --> 00:07:55,350
It's uncomfortable
having a boss's girlfriend around.

126
00:07:55,434 --> 00:07:56,268
What is it?

127
00:07:56,351 --> 00:07:57,186
It's nothing.

128
00:07:57,269 --> 00:07:59,021
-Just come by yourself.
-Okay.

129
00:08:13,118 --> 00:08:15,954
Don't tell a soul
that you gave those receipts to me.

130
00:08:16,038 --> 00:08:16,914
Understood?

131
00:08:20,042 --> 00:08:20,959
Geez.

132
00:08:26,048 --> 00:08:27,090
Mr. Noh.

133
00:08:29,384 --> 00:08:30,844
So this circus was your doing?

134
00:08:30,928 --> 00:08:32,346
I'm sorry, sir.

135
00:08:32,429 --> 00:08:33,931
If you want to strike, then do it right.

136
00:08:34,014 --> 00:08:36,516
Why do you always leave a job half-done?

137
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:40,354
If only Ms. Cha hadn't intervened,
this wouldn't have just blown over.

138
00:08:40,938 --> 00:08:43,607
And that's precisely why
you're so hopeless.

139
00:08:45,025 --> 00:08:48,779
What can you do if you're
stuck in the past and blind to reality?

140
00:08:51,573 --> 00:08:53,450
If you could give me one more chance…

141
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:54,952
No thanks.

142
00:08:56,662 --> 00:08:57,829
Don't ever call me again.

143
00:09:01,959 --> 00:09:02,960
Mr. Noh.

144
00:09:06,505 --> 00:09:07,339
Sir…

145
00:09:09,967 --> 00:09:13,595
So you're saying if we allow SAEUM
to set up a Home-AI Zone,

146
00:09:13,679 --> 00:09:17,015
you'll take on designing themed zones
for other companies as well?

147
00:09:17,099 --> 00:09:18,517
Yes, that's correct.

148
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:21,478
If that's the case,
there's no reason for us to say no.

149
00:09:24,898 --> 00:09:27,317
Then we'll report to our higher-ups
and get back to you.

150
00:09:27,401 --> 00:09:28,694
Sounds like a plan.

151
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:36,493
I was absolutely terrified
they'd turn us down.

152
00:09:36,576 --> 00:09:37,411
Thank goodness.

153
00:09:38,328 --> 00:09:39,871
We just need our executives on board now.

154
00:09:40,539 --> 00:09:41,498
Yes.

155
00:09:42,749 --> 00:09:44,167
Just relax and smile like that.

156
00:09:44,835 --> 00:09:47,879
And stop shutting
elevator doors in my face.

157
00:09:48,964 --> 00:09:49,840
Okay.

158
00:09:55,637 --> 00:09:57,014
Cha Ji-yoon's got guts, doesn't she?

159
00:09:57,723 --> 00:09:59,057
Dating Three-No-Man?

160
00:09:59,141 --> 00:10:01,893
-Hey, could you ever date a guy like him?
-Yeah.

161
00:10:02,519 --> 00:10:04,104
He's handsome and competent.

162
00:10:04,187 --> 00:10:05,480
There's no reason not to.

163
00:10:06,273 --> 00:10:07,274
Although he's divorced.

164
00:10:08,317 --> 00:10:10,610
Did Ji-yoon know all that
before they started dating?

165
00:10:10,694 --> 00:10:14,197
Well, I don't think
Mr. Kang would hide that stuff.

166
00:10:14,281 --> 00:10:17,034
Is there a chance
Cha Ji-yoon seduced him on purpose?

167
00:10:17,117 --> 00:10:19,077
Yeah, I seduced him.

168
00:10:19,953 --> 00:10:21,580
I can't believe you guys left me out.

169
00:10:23,457 --> 00:10:25,792
-Did you invite her?
-Yeah, it's a cohort hangout.

170
00:10:26,376 --> 00:10:27,753
I invited her as well.

171
00:10:27,836 --> 00:10:30,547
These guys said they feel awkward
drinking with you now.

172
00:10:30,630 --> 00:10:31,506
But why?

173
00:10:31,590 --> 00:10:33,008
Let's be real here.

174
00:10:33,091 --> 00:10:35,761
We meet up like this to blow off steam
by trashing our bosses.

175
00:10:36,428 --> 00:10:38,555
We can't do that
in front of a boss's girlfriend.

176
00:10:38,638 --> 00:10:41,099
Your boss isn't my boss,
so why do you care?

177
00:10:41,183 --> 00:10:42,559
Even so, word could travel up.

178
00:10:43,810 --> 00:10:45,604
We're way too busy talking about us.

179
00:10:45,687 --> 00:10:47,356
Wow, look at her saying "us" already.

180
00:10:48,315 --> 00:10:50,567
There's a silver lining
to Ji-yoon dating Mr. Kang.

181
00:10:51,193 --> 00:10:52,027
Like what?

182
00:10:52,110 --> 00:10:54,905
Remember when Mr. Kang first came here?

183
00:10:54,988 --> 00:10:56,782
Everyone was in hysteria,

184
00:10:56,865 --> 00:10:59,618
calling him the Grim Reaper
and saying there'll be a bloodbath.

185
00:11:00,494 --> 00:11:01,411
But look at him now.

186
00:11:01,495 --> 00:11:03,538
No one calls him Three-No-Man anymore.

187
00:11:04,164 --> 00:11:06,917
We're working in peace right now

188
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,294
all thanks to Ji-yoon, man.

189
00:11:09,378 --> 00:11:12,172
Does that mean Ji-yoon tamed Three-No-Man?

190
00:11:14,007 --> 00:11:16,009
You're darn right, I did.

191
00:11:16,093 --> 00:11:17,427
You're welcome, by the way.

192
00:11:17,511 --> 00:11:19,596
Now stop talking about me
and just drink up.

193
00:11:19,679 --> 00:11:20,514
Cheers!

194
00:11:20,597 --> 00:11:22,849
-Cheers!
-Cheers! Drink up!

195
00:11:28,772 --> 00:11:29,981
Man, I'm exhausted.

196
00:11:36,488 --> 00:11:38,365
I should still call him.

197
00:11:47,958 --> 00:11:49,251
Hi, Ms. Ji-yoon.

198
00:11:49,334 --> 00:11:51,670
Calling to report my safe return home.

199
00:11:52,921 --> 00:11:53,964
Did you drink a lot?

200
00:11:54,714 --> 00:11:55,549
Yes.

201
00:11:56,341 --> 00:11:59,136
Whenever I tried to hold back,
they said I'd changed.

202
00:11:59,219 --> 00:12:02,597
When I tried to drink up, they said
I was riding high on my relationship.

203
00:12:02,681 --> 00:12:05,475
So I gave up and drank like crazy.

204
00:12:06,351 --> 00:12:07,978
I should've come and picked you up.

205
00:12:08,061 --> 00:12:11,356
No way, I don't want them seeing
you pick up your girlfriend.

206
00:12:12,983 --> 00:12:14,401
What's wrong with everyone?

207
00:12:14,484 --> 00:12:16,111
I'm still the same,

208
00:12:16,570 --> 00:12:19,656
but they don't see me as Cha Ji-yoon.
Just as Kang Si-woo's girlfriend.

209
00:12:19,739 --> 00:12:22,284
Then make them see me
just as Cha Ji-yoon's boyfriend too.

210
00:12:23,493 --> 00:12:24,786
Deal.

211
00:12:24,870 --> 00:12:26,997
I'll just crush them all with pure talent.

212
00:12:32,919 --> 00:12:34,546
When I first heard
about her special promotion,

213
00:12:34,629 --> 00:12:37,549
I didn't think much of it
since she's good at her job.

214
00:12:37,632 --> 00:12:39,634
But thinking about it now, that's not it.

215
00:12:39,718 --> 00:12:41,470
She did everything with Mr. Kang,

216
00:12:41,553 --> 00:12:43,472
from the sphere ice refrigerator
to Home-AI.

217
00:12:44,014 --> 00:12:46,475
What if he intentionally
took her to his team from the start?

218
00:12:46,558 --> 00:12:47,934
Come on, no way.

219
00:12:48,018 --> 00:12:49,352
We all saw

220
00:12:49,436 --> 00:12:51,563
Ms. Cha fighting with Mr. Ko.

221
00:12:51,646 --> 00:12:53,148
That's why she left the team.

222
00:12:53,773 --> 00:12:56,318
Besides, no one wanted
to join the task force at first.

223
00:12:56,401 --> 00:12:58,153
That fight could've been part of the plan.

224
00:12:58,778 --> 00:13:01,448
Anyway, if anyone deserves
to be a Manager, it's you.

225
00:13:01,531 --> 00:13:03,366
It's ridiculous
for Ms. Cha to get the title first.

226
00:13:03,450 --> 00:13:04,534
Well, that's true.

227
00:13:05,202 --> 00:13:07,787
I was sure you'll be the next person
to become a Manager.

228
00:13:08,413 --> 00:13:11,291
Are you just going to
sit back and watch this happen?

229
00:13:11,374 --> 00:13:14,044
While Ms. Cha gets promoted,
thanks to her Manager boyfriend?

230
00:13:16,963 --> 00:13:18,215
If you're done, let's go in.

231
00:13:34,606 --> 00:13:37,526
YOU'RE REPULSIVE

232
00:13:46,201 --> 00:13:47,035
Shall we head out?

233
00:13:47,577 --> 00:13:48,411
Yes.

234
00:13:49,996 --> 00:13:51,540
Why do you look so nervous?

235
00:13:52,791 --> 00:13:54,876
Because I poured everything
into preparing this.

236
00:13:56,836 --> 00:13:58,755
You're going to crush it. Don't worry.

237
00:13:59,881 --> 00:14:00,715
Okay.

238
00:14:26,324 --> 00:14:28,743
Proposing themed zones for our competitors

239
00:14:28,827 --> 00:14:32,038
is not only a necessary choice
for our Home-AI Zone,

240
00:14:32,122 --> 00:14:34,416
but also a strategy
to expand our customer base.

241
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:38,503
A customer's journey
doesn't start with just one brand.

242
00:14:38,587 --> 00:14:42,340
Some might enter the store
drawn to a competitor's themed zone,

243
00:14:42,424 --> 00:14:45,176
but once they
experience SAEUM's Home-AI Zone,

244
00:14:45,260 --> 00:14:48,805
they will be won over
by the new technology we provide.

245
00:14:48,888 --> 00:14:49,723
Thank you.

246
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:57,272
Isn't that too naive?

247
00:14:57,355 --> 00:14:59,816
What if our competitors
end up outshining us?

248
00:14:59,899 --> 00:15:01,568
I'm confident that having

249
00:15:01,651 --> 00:15:05,322
a direct comparison will only make
SAEUM's Home-AI stand out even more.

250
00:15:06,740 --> 00:15:08,491
What's your take on this, Mr. Kang?

251
00:15:09,034 --> 00:15:10,243
It's an excellent proposal.

252
00:15:10,327 --> 00:15:12,162
It's a chance to expand the overall market

253
00:15:12,245 --> 00:15:16,291
and clearly demonstrate
why Home-AI is a necessity.

254
00:15:17,459 --> 00:15:18,501
Backing your girlfriend?

255
00:15:26,051 --> 00:15:29,721
Can you say with absolute certainty
that no personal feelings

256
00:15:29,804 --> 00:15:31,014
affected your judgment?

257
00:15:32,265 --> 00:15:33,433
I'm simply evaluating

258
00:15:34,100 --> 00:15:36,061
a team member's proposal as the team lead.

259
00:15:36,144 --> 00:15:38,146
Is it possible this was your own idea

260
00:15:38,229 --> 00:15:40,440
and you let Ms. Cha present it
on your behalf?

261
00:15:41,024 --> 00:15:42,317
Why would I even do that?

262
00:15:42,400 --> 00:15:44,819
You also had Ms. Cha
handle the presentation

263
00:15:44,903 --> 00:15:46,863
of the sphere ice refrigerator.

264
00:15:46,946 --> 00:15:48,281
The refrigerator and this plan

265
00:15:48,365 --> 00:15:51,785
both started from Ms. Cha's idea.

266
00:15:51,868 --> 00:15:54,871
Well, it's only human nature to want
to give more opportunities

267
00:15:54,954 --> 00:15:57,123
to an employee
you hold a special fondness for.

268
00:15:57,207 --> 00:15:58,583
That's unacceptable, though.

269
00:15:58,667 --> 00:15:59,793
That's favoritism.

270
00:15:59,876 --> 00:16:01,378
That's enough.

271
00:16:01,461 --> 00:16:04,714
I'm hearing more unnecessary comments
than actual feedback on the proposal.

272
00:16:04,798 --> 00:16:08,259
Her proposal was
so unrealistic that I wondered

273
00:16:08,343 --> 00:16:09,803
if someone was blindly backing her.

274
00:16:11,596 --> 00:16:13,390
This is way too risky.

275
00:16:13,473 --> 00:16:14,307
I say we reject it.

276
00:16:26,903 --> 00:16:28,279
Go back

277
00:16:28,363 --> 00:16:31,032
and find a safer, more realistic approach.

278
00:16:57,517 --> 00:16:59,811
I heard Cha Ji-yoon got chewed out
at the executive meeting.

279
00:16:59,894 --> 00:17:00,729
Really?

280
00:17:00,812 --> 00:17:02,772
They asked if Mr. Kang
had been pulling strings for her.

281
00:17:02,856 --> 00:17:04,566
How long have they been dating?

282
00:17:04,649 --> 00:17:05,692
Pretty long, I think.

283
00:17:05,775 --> 00:17:07,527
He definitely backed up his girlfriend.

284
00:17:07,610 --> 00:17:08,445
Favoritism?

285
00:17:08,528 --> 00:17:09,362
It's ridiculous

286
00:17:09,446 --> 00:17:11,948
Clock-out Fairy got promoted
because she bagged the right guy!

287
00:17:12,031 --> 00:17:14,117
You could say that's a skill too.

288
00:17:15,160 --> 00:17:16,161
I'll say it again.

289
00:17:16,244 --> 00:17:18,204
Your proposal was excellent.

290
00:17:18,288 --> 00:17:20,790
But the higher-ups always prefer

291
00:17:20,874 --> 00:17:23,585
a familiar method with proven success
over a new challenge.

292
00:17:24,210 --> 00:17:27,380
My proposal just wasn't
strong enough to break that wall.

293
00:17:54,032 --> 00:17:56,868
You should tune out
everyone else's words for a while.

294
00:17:56,951 --> 00:17:58,286
Focus on your own voice.

295
00:18:20,141 --> 00:18:22,769
Is there a chance
Cha Ji-yoon seduced him on purpose?

296
00:18:22,852 --> 00:18:26,689
Can you say with absolute certainty
that no personal feelings

297
00:18:26,773 --> 00:18:27,982
affected your judgment?

298
00:18:34,405 --> 00:18:38,743
YOU'RE REPULSIVE

299
00:18:54,634 --> 00:18:55,510
I love you.

300
00:19:18,324 --> 00:19:20,577
YOU'RE REPULSIVE

301
00:19:35,758 --> 00:19:36,759
Tastes good to me.

302
00:19:47,562 --> 00:19:51,441
HOME-AI THEMED POP-UP ZONE OPERATION PLAN

303
00:20:05,496 --> 00:20:06,873
There's nothing sexier

304
00:20:06,956 --> 00:20:09,042
than someone working hard at their job.

305
00:20:10,501 --> 00:20:11,669
Just give me one second.

306
00:20:11,753 --> 00:20:14,172
Don't mind me. It's fun watching you work.

307
00:20:17,967 --> 00:20:19,010
All done.

308
00:20:21,512 --> 00:20:23,932
Would you like the honor of being
the first to hear the finished track?

309
00:20:24,015 --> 00:20:25,350
Are you serious?

310
00:20:25,433 --> 00:20:26,267
Can I, really?

311
00:20:41,407 --> 00:20:42,492
This is wild.

312
00:20:42,575 --> 00:20:44,243
I can't believe my boyfriend made this.

313
00:20:44,327 --> 00:20:45,870
I only did the mixing, though.

314
00:20:46,496 --> 00:20:48,039
Mixing is the finishing touch.

315
00:20:48,122 --> 00:20:50,833
The one who finishes the job
is always the coolest.

316
00:21:02,428 --> 00:21:03,304
What's this?

317
00:21:04,973 --> 00:21:06,099
My finishing touch.

318
00:21:14,691 --> 00:21:15,525
Jae-in.

319
00:21:16,317 --> 00:21:17,902
I'll save the ring for later.

320
00:21:20,488 --> 00:21:22,031
I didn't see this coming at all.

321
00:21:25,660 --> 00:21:27,537
I never thought
I'd want to do stuff like this.

322
00:21:39,382 --> 00:21:40,258
It's gorgeous.

323
00:21:41,217 --> 00:21:42,677
Hey, you need to put mine on me too.

324
00:21:50,435 --> 00:21:51,352
Beautiful.

325
00:21:51,978 --> 00:21:54,022
Let's promise to stay together
until these snap.

326
00:21:56,607 --> 00:21:57,692
If…

327
00:21:58,693 --> 00:21:59,944
And it's a big if…

328
00:22:01,696 --> 00:22:04,699
What would you do if I got transferred
to an overseas office?

329
00:22:08,411 --> 00:22:09,954
I hate long-distance, so I'd follow you.

330
00:22:10,663 --> 00:22:11,539
Really?

331
00:22:11,622 --> 00:22:14,584
Just wait until I graduate.
I'll follow you to the ends of the Earth.

332
00:22:14,667 --> 00:22:17,962
But what if I had to leave immediately?

333
00:22:23,176 --> 00:22:24,594
Just thinking about that sucks.

334
00:22:25,303 --> 00:22:28,097
Let's cut out the horrible what-ifs
and take a selfie instead.

335
00:22:28,931 --> 00:22:29,807
Sure.

336
00:22:46,157 --> 00:22:47,450
The Admin Team employee in charge

337
00:22:47,533 --> 00:22:51,204
keeps insisting
they simply misplaced the receipts,

338
00:22:51,287 --> 00:22:52,747
so the investigation's hit a wall.

339
00:22:52,830 --> 00:22:53,664
On the bright side,

340
00:22:53,748 --> 00:22:56,709
the online forum is flooded with comments
calling out the post as fake,

341
00:22:56,793 --> 00:22:58,920
so people's negative feedback has been

342
00:22:59,003 --> 00:23:00,755
redirected to the post itself.

343
00:23:02,006 --> 00:23:05,426
What you're saying is
there's nothing the company can do.

344
00:23:07,220 --> 00:23:08,054
So what, then?

345
00:23:08,763 --> 00:23:10,932
I doubt you called this meeting
just to tell me that.

346
00:23:11,641 --> 00:23:13,935
There's been a formal complaint
filed against you.

347
00:23:15,144 --> 00:23:15,978
What does it say?

348
00:23:16,062 --> 00:23:18,856
It alleges you've been
providing special treatment

349
00:23:18,940 --> 00:23:20,566
to your girlfriend, Ms. Cha.

350
00:23:24,946 --> 00:23:27,698
Mr. Kang's reputation
is at a critical low these days.

351
00:23:27,782 --> 00:23:29,826
He's dragging down
the company's image with him.

352
00:23:29,909 --> 00:23:30,827
You have to do something.

353
00:23:30,910 --> 00:23:33,704
His alleged relationship
with Ms. Choi Soo-jin has been

354
00:23:33,788 --> 00:23:35,665
proven false through various channels.

355
00:23:35,748 --> 00:23:37,750
Let's not make an issue of it any further.

356
00:23:37,834 --> 00:23:39,377
Well, an affair is

357
00:23:39,460 --> 00:23:42,088
a private matter
without a direct victim after all,

358
00:23:42,171 --> 00:23:43,923
so the company can't interfere.

359
00:23:44,006 --> 00:23:46,425
But allegations of favoritism
is a different story.

360
00:23:46,509 --> 00:23:48,803
Now that a formal complaint
has been filed,

361
00:23:49,428 --> 00:23:51,222
the company can't just turn a blind eye.

362
00:23:51,305 --> 00:23:53,474
As you said, it's just an allegation.

363
00:23:54,016 --> 00:23:56,936
HR is looking into it as we speak,

364
00:23:57,019 --> 00:23:58,062
so let's wait and see.

365
00:23:59,021 --> 00:24:01,941
Were you two dating
during the performance review period?

366
00:24:02,733 --> 00:24:03,568
No.

367
00:24:03,651 --> 00:24:07,780
The sphere ice refrigerator presentation
was the basis for your review on her.

368
00:24:07,864 --> 00:24:09,907
Did your personal feelings affect it?

369
00:24:09,991 --> 00:24:12,910
If you're asking if my romantic feelings
for her affected the review,

370
00:24:13,077 --> 00:24:14,245
then no.

371
00:24:14,871 --> 00:24:16,289
Let me ask you again.

372
00:24:18,666 --> 00:24:20,751
Was your performance review on Ms. Cha

373
00:24:20,835 --> 00:24:22,128
unbiased and fair?

374
00:24:23,045 --> 00:24:24,255
Yes.

375
00:24:24,338 --> 00:24:29,177
Fairness is the most sensitive issue
among our employees right now.

376
00:24:30,303 --> 00:24:32,471
If they start thinking
that things aren't fair,

377
00:24:32,555 --> 00:24:34,849
they won't trust anything
the company does.

378
00:24:35,850 --> 00:24:36,726
So?

379
00:24:38,019 --> 00:24:40,313
What's the solution you're suggesting?

380
00:24:41,355 --> 00:24:44,025
We need to get rid
of the root cause of the allegations.

381
00:24:49,780 --> 00:24:51,115
What brings you here?

382
00:24:54,785 --> 00:24:57,580
It's the revised design draft
for the Home-AI refrigerator.

383
00:24:57,663 --> 00:24:59,248
REFRIGERATOR SCREEN DESIGN REVISIONS

384
00:25:00,082 --> 00:25:00,917
But why?

385
00:25:03,336 --> 00:25:07,423
I revised the design
after listening to Ms. Cha's feedback.

386
00:25:09,508 --> 00:25:10,843
That's favoritism too, right?

387
00:25:13,221 --> 00:25:16,307
She works tirelessly for the company,
so stop tormenting her.

388
00:25:16,390 --> 00:25:19,685
Mr. Kang, myself, and all of SAEUM

389
00:25:19,769 --> 00:25:21,938
are actually the ones
benefiting from Ms. Cha.

390
00:25:22,605 --> 00:25:25,524
We may all be tiny screws in a big system,
but some shine brighter.

391
00:25:25,608 --> 00:25:27,109
So do you really think

392
00:25:28,736 --> 00:25:30,404
appreciating her talent is favoritism?

393
00:25:32,990 --> 00:25:34,367
I suggest we make Manager Kang

394
00:25:35,576 --> 00:25:37,912
step down
from the task force's team lead position.

395
00:26:03,938 --> 00:26:06,274
A permanent installation
is out of the question now.

396
00:26:06,357 --> 00:26:08,109
How about we pitch it as a pop-up?

397
00:26:08,734 --> 00:26:11,404
I don't know.
A pop-up will be a tough sell too.

398
00:26:11,487 --> 00:26:13,531
We still have to try.

399
00:26:13,614 --> 00:26:15,032
Without a physical installation,

400
00:26:15,116 --> 00:26:17,493
we can't properly showcase
our Home-AI products.

401
00:26:17,576 --> 00:26:18,995
All right. Let's do it.

402
00:26:24,458 --> 00:26:26,210
Someone filed a complaint
against Mr. Kang.

403
00:26:26,294 --> 00:26:27,461
A complaint? For what?

404
00:26:30,381 --> 00:26:32,717
Allegations of favoritism toward Ms. Cha.

405
00:26:32,800 --> 00:26:33,926
That's complete garbage!

406
00:26:34,010 --> 00:26:36,304
Then what about me?
Was I unfairly favored too?

407
00:26:36,387 --> 00:26:37,471
I know.

408
00:26:39,390 --> 00:26:41,017
My arrogant action has come back

409
00:26:42,226 --> 00:26:43,769
to hit me like a boomerang.

410
00:26:55,614 --> 00:26:57,533
You'd always keep
your head down and work.

411
00:26:58,367 --> 00:26:59,952
But why is there so much noise these days?

412
00:27:01,829 --> 00:27:02,997
I'm sorry, ma'am.

413
00:27:07,126 --> 00:27:08,669
An apology? That's so unlike you.

414
00:27:10,629 --> 00:27:11,756
The biggest reason

415
00:27:12,798 --> 00:27:15,760
why I chose to bring you
into my inner circle was because

416
00:27:15,843 --> 00:27:18,262
you never did anything
that you had to apologize for.

417
00:27:18,846 --> 00:27:20,306
But you know very well

418
00:27:21,223 --> 00:27:22,475
the allegations aren't true.

419
00:27:24,352 --> 00:27:25,478
As for Ms. Cha,

420
00:27:26,354 --> 00:27:28,606
let's settle it
by canceling her special promotion.

421
00:27:28,689 --> 00:27:31,025
We'll transfer her
to another office after the launch.

422
00:27:31,108 --> 00:27:33,444
If there's a problem,
I'll take any punishment.

423
00:27:33,527 --> 00:27:34,445
I'll transfer instead.

424
00:27:34,528 --> 00:27:35,404
I cannot…

425
00:27:37,573 --> 00:27:38,699
afford to lose you too.

426
00:28:15,611 --> 00:28:17,655
Someone filed a complaint
against Mr. Kang.

427
00:28:20,032 --> 00:28:22,410
Allegations of favoritism toward Ms. Cha.

428
00:28:54,108 --> 00:28:55,484
Thank you.

429
00:28:55,568 --> 00:28:56,610
I'll let you two talk.

430
00:29:04,368 --> 00:29:05,703
What did HR say?

431
00:29:05,786 --> 00:29:08,581
You won't get hit with anything, right?

432
00:29:10,499 --> 00:29:12,710
Let's talk about something
other than work.

433
00:29:13,544 --> 00:29:15,212
It's the end of the year.
What do you want to do?

434
00:29:16,839 --> 00:29:19,300
Maybe going on a trip or seeing a show?

435
00:29:20,342 --> 00:29:21,594
Should we book a nice dinner?

436
00:29:23,137 --> 00:29:25,389
The launch is
all I can think about right now.

437
00:29:27,016 --> 00:29:28,476
So it's back to work again.

438
00:29:30,060 --> 00:29:31,520
Do you love work that much?

439
00:29:32,021 --> 00:29:34,106
Well, I just enjoy what I do.

440
00:29:34,190 --> 00:29:36,484
Planning a new product that doesn't exist,

441
00:29:36,567 --> 00:29:39,028
collaborating with other teams
to create a product

442
00:29:39,111 --> 00:29:41,864
that people will love and releasing it.

443
00:29:41,947 --> 00:29:44,408
You must have a lot of ideas
for the future too.

444
00:29:44,492 --> 00:29:46,952
If you're worried about
what to work on next,

445
00:29:47,036 --> 00:29:48,162
then don't be.

446
00:29:48,662 --> 00:29:50,164
My head is full of ideas.

447
00:29:50,247 --> 00:29:51,999
If you want to launch all that,

448
00:29:52,082 --> 00:29:54,460
you'll have to stay in your job
for a very long time.

449
00:29:54,543 --> 00:29:55,377
Exactly.

450
00:29:56,086 --> 00:29:58,589
I want to do all of them with you.

451
00:29:59,840 --> 00:30:01,675
That's why I'm going to

452
00:30:01,759 --> 00:30:03,886
keep my distance from you
at work for a while.

453
00:30:03,969 --> 00:30:06,055
That way, I can work with you longer.

454
00:30:15,147 --> 00:30:16,065
I'm sorry.

455
00:30:17,191 --> 00:30:18,234
It really is favoritism,

456
00:30:19,068 --> 00:30:21,695
seeing I'm the only one you say sorry to.

457
00:30:34,124 --> 00:30:36,168
SPECIAL PROMOTION ANNOUNCEMENT
FOR SECOND HALF OF 2025

458
00:30:38,170 --> 00:30:41,382
SPECIAL PROMOTION LIST
NAME: JEON KEE-TAE

459
00:30:48,931 --> 00:30:50,558
PROMOTED TO: SR. ASSOCIATE

460
00:30:59,483 --> 00:31:00,317
I'm sorry.

461
00:31:04,238 --> 00:31:05,447
This makes no sense.

462
00:31:05,948 --> 00:31:08,659
You should go to HR
and find out what happened.

463
00:31:08,742 --> 00:31:10,911
I know what their answer will be.

464
00:31:13,163 --> 00:31:14,832
"We can't disclose that information."

465
00:31:14,915 --> 00:31:16,125
But still!

466
00:31:16,208 --> 00:31:17,793
This is so unfair.

467
00:31:19,920 --> 00:31:21,630
I'm going to step out for some air.

468
00:31:24,800 --> 00:31:25,634
I'll come with you.

469
00:31:26,719 --> 00:31:28,971
No, I want to be alone for a bit.

470
00:31:37,438 --> 00:31:39,315
Ms. Cha must be so upset.

471
00:31:40,649 --> 00:31:42,026
Congratulations, Mr. Jeon.

472
00:31:43,402 --> 00:31:45,654
I don't know
if I should be happy right now.

473
00:31:51,410 --> 00:31:54,580
Oh dear! My goodness.

474
00:31:55,164 --> 00:31:58,250
What a shame. To be let down like that.

475
00:31:59,043 --> 00:32:00,336
Thank you for your concern.

476
00:32:01,670 --> 00:32:03,714
Did you think it'd be easier to climb up

477
00:32:03,797 --> 00:32:05,674
by riding your boyfriend's coattails?

478
00:32:05,758 --> 00:32:07,301
It's actually the opposite.

479
00:32:07,885 --> 00:32:09,762
If you stay with Kang Si-woo,

480
00:32:09,845 --> 00:32:12,264
those allegations of favoritism
will follow you forever

481
00:32:12,348 --> 00:32:13,599
and you'll only get set back.

482
00:32:14,558 --> 00:32:15,517
That's fine.

483
00:32:16,268 --> 00:32:18,979
It's still a lot better
than the setbacks I faced

484
00:32:19,563 --> 00:32:20,648
when I worked under you.

485
00:32:21,482 --> 00:32:22,316
What?

486
00:32:22,399 --> 00:32:24,026
You stole your subordinates' ideas

487
00:32:24,735 --> 00:32:28,197
and bullied them so that you can take
all the achievements for yourself.

488
00:32:28,781 --> 00:32:30,324
You're the worst boss I've ever had.

489
00:32:41,293 --> 00:32:42,378
Ms. Cha!

490
00:32:44,963 --> 00:32:46,632
Ms. Cha, are you okay?

491
00:32:46,715 --> 00:32:47,758
Oh, no.

492
00:32:47,841 --> 00:32:48,926
-Are you okay?
-Get lost.

493
00:32:51,512 --> 00:32:52,638
What did you just say?

494
00:32:53,347 --> 00:32:54,431
The worst boss?

495
00:32:55,182 --> 00:32:56,975
Who the hell do you think you are,

496
00:32:57,059 --> 00:32:58,477
you ungrateful brat?

497
00:32:58,560 --> 00:33:01,188
I told you this before,
but you seem to keep forgetting.

498
00:33:01,980 --> 00:33:03,357
Using your rank and authority

499
00:33:03,440 --> 00:33:07,236
to cause physical or mental suffering
to another employee is a violation

500
00:33:07,319 --> 00:33:08,529
of the Labor Standards Act.

501
00:33:09,947 --> 00:33:10,781
So what?

502
00:33:11,365 --> 00:33:13,617
I'm going to report you.

503
00:33:16,578 --> 00:33:18,372
Have you lost your flipping mind?

504
00:33:18,455 --> 00:33:19,581
That's enough.

505
00:33:26,171 --> 00:33:27,423
Why? What is it?

506
00:33:30,926 --> 00:33:33,887
-Can't stand seeing your girl like this?
-She's a member of my team.

507
00:33:35,305 --> 00:33:36,390
I can tolerate you roughing me up

508
00:33:36,473 --> 00:33:39,643
and kicking me out of the team
for exposing your corruption.

509
00:33:39,727 --> 00:33:41,437
I won't tolerate you bullying my people

510
00:33:41,937 --> 00:33:42,980
any longer.

511
00:33:43,731 --> 00:33:45,107
So what, then?

512
00:33:45,190 --> 00:33:46,316
What can you even do?

513
00:33:46,900 --> 00:33:49,486
I noticed you've been
playing a lot of golf lately.

514
00:33:50,070 --> 00:33:51,655
I'm planning to look into

515
00:33:51,739 --> 00:33:54,658
who you've played it with so frequently
and for what reasons.

516
00:33:58,078 --> 00:33:59,496
What? You got any proof?

517
00:34:00,664 --> 00:34:02,124
If there's no proof, I'll fabricate it.

518
00:34:03,584 --> 00:34:06,462
Just like you fabricated a fake affair.

519
00:34:14,595 --> 00:34:16,013
Go ahead, try me.

520
00:34:16,513 --> 00:34:18,807
I can't wait to watch
the high-and-mighty Kang Si-woo

521
00:34:18,891 --> 00:34:21,643
play dirty for once.

522
00:34:32,362 --> 00:34:33,572
Damn it!

523
00:35:05,395 --> 00:35:07,314
What on earth is "fair" anyway?

524
00:35:08,440 --> 00:35:13,195
I'm facing setbacks because
of my relationship. Is that fair?

525
00:35:14,363 --> 00:35:17,324
Is it right to be forced to feel guilty

526
00:35:18,367 --> 00:35:19,326
just for loving someone?

527
00:35:21,537 --> 00:35:23,747
It's okay to be angry if you feel wronged.

528
00:35:23,831 --> 00:35:25,916
You can scream until you feel better.

529
00:35:27,376 --> 00:35:28,293
Can I really?

530
00:35:29,044 --> 00:35:29,920
Yes.

531
00:35:35,676 --> 00:35:38,303
Why can't you
just freaking leave me alone? Damn it!

532
00:35:38,387 --> 00:35:39,972
I feel wronged too, you know!

533
00:35:40,055 --> 00:35:43,725
What's so wrong about being competent
and having a good love life too?

534
00:35:43,809 --> 00:35:47,104
Are you any better?
Who are you to judge me?

535
00:35:47,187 --> 00:35:48,605
You bunch of crazy bastards!

536
00:35:55,362 --> 00:35:56,196
Whatever.

537
00:35:56,280 --> 00:35:57,823
It's only a promotion.

538
00:35:57,906 --> 00:35:59,908
If I can't get it now,
I'll get it next time.

539
00:36:00,617 --> 00:36:02,035
So please,

540
00:36:02,119 --> 00:36:04,788
stop apologizing to me
and blaming yourself.

541
00:36:05,539 --> 00:36:08,041
I'm holding myself back
from saying "Sorry" too.

542
00:36:15,132 --> 00:36:16,633
Hey, we're still at work.

543
00:36:20,137 --> 00:36:21,430
Work hours are over.

544
00:36:21,513 --> 00:36:22,598
It's past 6 p.m.

545
00:36:26,143 --> 00:36:27,853
Then let us clock out on the dot today.

546
00:37:12,356 --> 00:37:13,398
Thank you.

547
00:37:18,612 --> 00:37:19,446
Look…

548
00:37:20,656 --> 00:37:23,617
I know there's talk
about unfair favoritism or whatever,

549
00:37:24,660 --> 00:37:25,994
but not everyone thinks that way.

550
00:37:28,538 --> 00:37:32,250
Everyone knows how good you are
at your job, Ms. Cha.

551
00:37:33,961 --> 00:37:37,381
They're just jealous
because you have a good boss.

552
00:37:38,882 --> 00:37:40,175
You just

553
00:37:40,842 --> 00:37:42,302
keep doing your thing.

554
00:37:47,891 --> 00:37:49,393
Right, then. See you.

555
00:38:02,614 --> 00:38:05,575
It felt like a summer day
after a raging storm.

556
00:38:09,663 --> 00:38:10,789
And…

557
00:38:11,915 --> 00:38:13,667
our life just continued on,

558
00:38:15,460 --> 00:38:17,671
as if nothing had ever happened.

559
00:38:21,049 --> 00:38:22,009
At least…

560
00:38:24,261 --> 00:38:25,429
on the surface.

561
00:38:27,597 --> 00:38:28,640
It's time for the meeting.

562
00:38:28,724 --> 00:38:30,100
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

563
00:38:46,783 --> 00:38:49,286
So we're all set
for the overseas stores, right?

564
00:38:49,369 --> 00:38:50,203
Right.

565
00:38:50,287 --> 00:38:53,040
Now we just have to sort out
the domestic stores.

566
00:38:57,085 --> 00:38:58,378
HOME-AI THEMED POP-UP ZONE OPERATION PLAN

567
00:38:58,462 --> 00:39:00,839
They agreed
to host our Home-AI Zone as a pop-up

568
00:39:00,922 --> 00:39:03,175
for one month following our launch.

569
00:39:04,051 --> 00:39:06,428
I'd have given up
after getting my proposal rejected,

570
00:39:07,345 --> 00:39:09,139
but you actually brought an alternative.

571
00:39:09,222 --> 00:39:10,348
I was determined

572
00:39:10,432 --> 00:39:12,809
to set up the Home-AI Zone,
even for a short time.

573
00:39:13,393 --> 00:39:14,394
Don't you feel bad that

574
00:39:14,895 --> 00:39:17,814
your old proposal on the Home-AI Zone
and themed zones went to pot?

575
00:39:18,565 --> 00:39:19,566
I'm fine.

576
00:39:20,484 --> 00:39:21,860
I can just try again next time.

577
00:39:22,611 --> 00:39:26,198
When that time comes,
I will absolutely win everyone over.

578
00:39:28,909 --> 00:39:30,619
SIGNATURE

579
00:39:32,412 --> 00:39:33,830
Please proceed.

580
00:39:33,914 --> 00:39:34,915
Yes, ma'am.

581
00:39:45,175 --> 00:39:46,384
She's too good to waste.

582
00:39:51,515 --> 00:39:52,641
Sir,

583
00:39:52,724 --> 00:39:54,101
another complaint just came in.

584
00:39:55,393 --> 00:39:56,311
Manager Kang Si-woo again?

585
00:39:57,145 --> 00:39:59,189
No, it's about
Manager Ko Young-sam this time.

586
00:40:03,193 --> 00:40:04,069
What does it say?

587
00:40:04,694 --> 00:40:06,530
Workplace harassment through verbal abuse.

588
00:40:06,613 --> 00:40:08,365
REPORTING REPEATED WORKPLACE HARASSMENT
FROM MANAGER KO YOUNG-SAM

589
00:40:08,448 --> 00:40:10,117
There's even a voice recording here.

590
00:40:12,828 --> 00:40:13,662
Play it.

591
00:40:13,745 --> 00:40:14,746
Yes, sir.

592
00:40:16,748 --> 00:40:20,043
How many times do I have to tell you
to report things like that right away?!

593
00:40:20,127 --> 00:40:21,711
Do you all come to work for fun?

594
00:40:21,795 --> 00:40:23,171
Am I the only one working here?

595
00:40:23,255 --> 00:40:26,466
If you're going to act like this,
cough up your salaries or just quit!

596
00:40:26,550 --> 00:40:28,260
What did you just say?

597
00:40:28,343 --> 00:40:29,761
The worst boss?

598
00:40:29,845 --> 00:40:32,389
Who the hell do you think you are,

599
00:40:32,472 --> 00:40:33,557
you ungrateful brat?

600
00:40:33,640 --> 00:40:35,308
Have you lost your flipping mind?

601
00:40:35,892 --> 00:40:36,893
That's enough.

602
00:40:37,435 --> 00:40:38,270
Is it anonymous?

603
00:40:38,353 --> 00:40:39,354
No.

604
00:40:40,021 --> 00:40:42,858
It's from Associate Yoon No-ah
from Product Planning Team 1.

605
00:40:43,567 --> 00:40:46,194
If she didn't go anonymous,
then he's dead to rights.

606
00:40:47,529 --> 00:40:48,905
Ask Mr. Ko for an interview.

607
00:40:48,989 --> 00:40:49,906
Yes, sir.

608
00:40:58,081 --> 00:40:59,291
Did you do it?

609
00:41:05,172 --> 00:41:08,300
If you're talking
about the formal complaint against you,

610
00:41:09,009 --> 00:41:10,260
then yes, it was me.

611
00:41:13,346 --> 00:41:15,515
RECORDING

612
00:41:15,599 --> 00:41:17,601
Go tell them right now that it's not true.

613
00:41:17,684 --> 00:41:18,852
Why should I do that?

614
00:41:18,935 --> 00:41:20,353
Because it's not true at all!

615
00:41:22,189 --> 00:41:24,065
Do you think I did that to harass you?

616
00:41:24,566 --> 00:41:28,069
I was motivating everyone to work harder
for the good of the team and the company!

617
00:41:28,153 --> 00:41:29,070
No.

618
00:41:29,154 --> 00:41:31,072
You constantly treated us

619
00:41:31,156 --> 00:41:33,200
like we were completely worthless.

620
00:41:33,283 --> 00:41:34,201
You little…

621
00:41:38,496 --> 00:41:41,249
You think you can
cruise through this company after this?

622
00:41:41,333 --> 00:41:43,126
You think I'm going to
let you off the hook?

623
00:41:43,210 --> 00:41:44,836
Well, I'm going to Senegal!

624
00:41:46,087 --> 00:41:47,088
What?

625
00:41:55,305 --> 00:41:56,139
Ms. Cha.

626
00:41:56,765 --> 00:41:57,849
Mr. Kim!

627
00:41:59,392 --> 00:42:01,478
You won't even
show your face around the lab

628
00:42:01,561 --> 00:42:03,396
now that development's over, huh?

629
00:42:03,480 --> 00:42:08,151
Huh? If I came looking for you now,
that would mean it's a major emergency.

630
00:42:08,235 --> 00:42:09,110
Would you be okay?

631
00:42:10,237 --> 00:42:11,988
Just hearing that makes my palms sweat.

632
00:42:13,240 --> 00:42:14,449
Don't make jokes like that.

633
00:42:15,867 --> 00:42:18,078
Actually, I wanted to ask.

634
00:42:19,120 --> 00:42:21,915
I'm going to be the team lead
for the Future Tech Development Team.

635
00:42:22,874 --> 00:42:24,251
And I'd like you to join me.

636
00:42:33,051 --> 00:42:33,927
No, come on.

637
00:42:35,553 --> 00:42:37,722
How could I join the Development Team?

638
00:42:37,806 --> 00:42:40,809
Hey, you have a master's degree
in engineering, don't you?

639
00:42:40,892 --> 00:42:42,686
You being in Product Planning is weirder.

640
00:42:42,769 --> 00:42:46,231
Even so, it's work
I've been doing for seven years.

641
00:42:46,314 --> 00:42:47,232
Exactly.

642
00:42:47,899 --> 00:42:49,943
That work is why I'm asking you to join.

643
00:42:50,527 --> 00:42:51,486
You know very well

644
00:42:51,569 --> 00:42:53,989
how much the Planning Team
and Development Team fight.

645
00:42:54,072 --> 00:42:57,409
The Planning Team brings
impossible ideas and demands we make them,

646
00:42:57,492 --> 00:43:00,036
while the Development Team
just insists we can't do it.

647
00:43:00,912 --> 00:43:03,498
You're the only one
that understands both parties, Ms. Cha.

648
00:43:03,581 --> 00:43:05,917
You're the only planner who can make

649
00:43:06,001 --> 00:43:07,377
the impossible happen.

650
00:43:07,460 --> 00:43:11,756
My gosh, I get you're trying
to lift my mood, but that's too much.

651
00:43:11,840 --> 00:43:13,842
You know I'm a sucker for compliments.

652
00:43:14,426 --> 00:43:16,469
I'm being serious here.

653
00:43:17,804 --> 00:43:19,180
Think about it, okay?

654
00:43:21,308 --> 00:43:22,517
Okay.

655
00:43:22,600 --> 00:43:23,601
Thank you.

656
00:43:45,790 --> 00:43:47,375
Now that's the best stress-reliever.

657
00:43:50,545 --> 00:43:51,421
You know,

658
00:43:52,630 --> 00:43:53,715
I got a job offer today.

659
00:43:54,883 --> 00:43:55,717
From where?

660
00:43:55,800 --> 00:43:57,552
The Future Tech Development Team.

661
00:43:58,053 --> 00:43:59,763
Mr. Kim himself asked me to join.

662
00:43:59,846 --> 00:44:01,056
The Development Team?

663
00:44:01,848 --> 00:44:03,767
But you love what you're doing now.

664
00:44:04,517 --> 00:44:05,643
That is true,

665
00:44:06,353 --> 00:44:07,395
but hey…

666
00:44:07,479 --> 00:44:10,482
You can't only do
what you want to do at work.

667
00:44:10,565 --> 00:44:13,735
When things get rough,
you have to look at your options.

668
00:44:17,739 --> 00:44:18,823
By "rough things,"

669
00:44:19,449 --> 00:44:20,492
do you mean me?

670
00:44:20,575 --> 00:44:23,370
Come on. It's not you, it's us.

671
00:44:24,954 --> 00:44:27,415
I want to handle both my career

672
00:44:27,499 --> 00:44:29,417
and my love life wisely.

673
00:44:33,338 --> 00:44:35,131
Oh, did you hear?

674
00:44:35,882 --> 00:44:37,550
Besides No-ah,
other people also sent in

675
00:44:37,634 --> 00:44:39,260
recordings of Mr. Ko's verbal abuse.

676
00:44:40,387 --> 00:44:41,679
You filed a report too, right?

677
00:44:41,763 --> 00:44:43,056
Of course, I did.

678
00:44:43,139 --> 00:44:44,849
Serves him right, huh?

679
00:44:47,519 --> 00:44:50,146
I can trash my boss
since we're outside the office, right?

680
00:44:50,730 --> 00:44:52,607
Didn't you already do that
to the company fridge?

681
00:44:52,690 --> 00:44:54,234
Hey, I only did that

682
00:44:54,734 --> 00:44:57,320
because my direct superior made me do it.

683
00:45:00,615 --> 00:45:01,741
Just try it.

684
00:45:07,705 --> 00:45:08,540
It's good, isn't it?

685
00:45:08,623 --> 00:45:09,582
It's good.

686
00:45:19,634 --> 00:45:21,052
Do you love work that much?

687
00:45:21,636 --> 00:45:23,888
Well, I just enjoy what I do.

688
00:45:23,972 --> 00:45:25,807
What on earth is "fair" anyway?

689
00:45:25,890 --> 00:45:31,479
I'm facing setbacks because
of my relationship. Is that fair?

690
00:45:31,563 --> 00:45:32,856
As for Ms. Cha,

691
00:45:32,939 --> 00:45:34,899
let's settle it by canceling
her special promotion.

692
00:45:34,983 --> 00:45:37,068
You know, I got a job offer today.

693
00:45:56,713 --> 00:45:59,799
Then please film it and send the video
as soon as it's finished.

694
00:46:00,300 --> 00:46:01,759
Yes, thank you.

695
00:46:01,843 --> 00:46:04,095
Did you check the status of all stores?

696
00:46:04,179 --> 00:46:06,598
I confirmed that all products
have been delivered.

697
00:46:06,681 --> 00:46:08,266
The Sales Team members at each store

698
00:46:08,349 --> 00:46:10,643
will check the Home-AI Zones
and send video updates.

699
00:46:10,727 --> 00:46:11,603
Great.

700
00:46:12,187 --> 00:46:14,481
Did you make sure
no press or partner companies

701
00:46:14,564 --> 00:46:15,899
missed their video invitation?

702
00:46:15,982 --> 00:46:18,985
Yes, I double-checked that, but…

703
00:46:22,030 --> 00:46:24,115
The web drama series
hasn't been uploaded yet.

704
00:46:24,199 --> 00:46:25,909
Check with the Marketing Team again.

705
00:46:25,992 --> 00:46:26,868
Yes, sir.

706
00:46:29,871 --> 00:46:31,664
-Food's here.
-Hello.

707
00:46:31,748 --> 00:46:33,458
This is Shin Na-ri from the task force.

708
00:46:35,543 --> 00:46:36,920
Yes, this is Jeon Kee-tae.

709
00:46:38,755 --> 00:46:40,089
What's wrong with the server?

710
00:46:41,049 --> 00:46:43,092
You know how important online sales are.

711
00:46:43,176 --> 00:46:45,261
You have to restore it right now. Yes.

712
00:46:45,345 --> 00:46:47,013
Okay, I'll check it too. Bye.

713
00:46:48,932 --> 00:46:50,225
What should we do?

714
00:46:50,308 --> 00:46:52,477
They haven't finished
editing the web series.

715
00:46:53,353 --> 00:46:54,854
We still have some time left.

716
00:46:54,938 --> 00:46:56,689
Keep following up until it's uploaded.

717
00:46:56,773 --> 00:46:57,649
Yes, sir.

718
00:47:00,527 --> 00:47:02,278
This is Cha Ji-yoon from the task force.

719
00:47:03,988 --> 00:47:04,948
Yes.

720
00:47:05,031 --> 00:47:05,990
Yes, that's right.

721
00:47:08,326 --> 00:47:10,328
Yes, I'll email that to you right away.

722
00:47:15,708 --> 00:47:17,710
I can't believe this day actually came.

723
00:47:19,379 --> 00:47:23,007
Our babies must be
filling up all the stores, right?

724
00:47:23,591 --> 00:47:27,595
And President Han
must've landed in Las Vegas.

725
00:47:29,180 --> 00:47:30,348
But Mr. Kang,

726
00:47:31,558 --> 00:47:33,685
why didn't you go to CES?

727
00:47:34,352 --> 00:47:37,730
You should've gone so we could tag along.

728
00:47:38,314 --> 00:47:40,191
If you think back to last night,

729
00:47:40,275 --> 00:47:41,651
you'd know why I didn't go.

730
00:47:41,734 --> 00:47:42,610
True.

731
00:47:43,403 --> 00:47:44,904
We burned the midnight oil.

732
00:47:45,613 --> 00:47:47,407
Still, you're the star of this project.

733
00:47:47,490 --> 00:47:49,325
It's a shame you're missing the spotlight.

734
00:47:49,409 --> 00:47:50,994
I'm not the star here.

735
00:47:51,703 --> 00:47:52,704
-It's us, right?
-It's us, right?

736
00:47:53,288 --> 00:47:54,414
No.

737
00:47:54,497 --> 00:47:55,331
-The company.
-The company.

738
00:47:56,666 --> 00:47:57,667
Ms. Cha.

739
00:47:57,750 --> 00:48:00,503
It feels like you're becoming
like Mr. Kang more and more.

740
00:48:01,713 --> 00:48:02,922
"Three-No-Girl."

741
00:48:03,006 --> 00:48:06,134
And Mr. Kang is becoming
like Ms. Cha more and more.

742
00:48:06,217 --> 00:48:08,303
I can't be the Clock-out Fairy,

743
00:48:08,386 --> 00:48:10,096
but I can be the Clock-in Fairy.

744
00:48:13,308 --> 00:48:14,142
It's starting!

745
00:48:22,275 --> 00:48:24,444
I gave it my all again today.

746
00:48:27,947 --> 00:48:29,198
What I need right now

747
00:48:31,159 --> 00:48:31,993
is home,

748
00:48:33,828 --> 00:48:35,038
and AI.

749
00:48:35,622 --> 00:48:37,498
Curious about
homebody Cho Ga-eul's daily life?

750
00:48:37,582 --> 00:48:39,834
Look up the web drama series, SAEUM Villa.

751
00:48:40,543 --> 00:48:43,004
I recharge myself with Home-AI.

752
00:48:44,255 --> 00:48:47,508
I totally became a fan of Cho Ga-eul
because of this.

753
00:48:47,592 --> 00:48:50,261
I genuinely don't understand
why he's so popular.

754
00:48:50,345 --> 00:48:52,305
He's so handsome!

755
00:48:52,388 --> 00:48:53,765
He's a good singer too.

756
00:48:54,265 --> 00:48:57,685
I saw him at the shoot for the series,
and he was super polite too.

757
00:48:57,769 --> 00:48:59,979
My wife plays his songs
nonstop these days.

758
00:49:00,063 --> 00:49:01,397
It's driving me insane.

759
00:49:02,106 --> 00:49:03,358
His song's pretty good, though.

760
00:49:04,192 --> 00:49:05,818
You listened to it too, Mr. Kang?

761
00:49:05,902 --> 00:49:07,028
I listen to music, you know.

762
00:49:08,071 --> 00:49:09,197
I see.

763
00:49:10,156 --> 00:49:12,617
I hope everything
works out well for everyone.

764
00:49:14,077 --> 00:49:14,911
Yes.

765
00:49:16,871 --> 00:49:17,705
It will.

766
00:49:49,320 --> 00:49:50,321
This is so cozy.

767
00:49:51,280 --> 00:49:52,740
It's freezing outside today.

768
00:49:52,824 --> 00:49:56,077
If I'd walked to our usual spot,
I would've turned into a popsicle.

769
00:49:57,954 --> 00:49:59,080
Seatbelt.

770
00:50:05,461 --> 00:50:07,004
We're right in front of our office.

771
00:50:07,088 --> 00:50:09,674
You're getting bolder by the day,
aren't you, Ms. Cha?

772
00:50:09,757 --> 00:50:11,592
I've got nothing to fear now.

773
00:50:12,802 --> 00:50:14,303
I lost the special promotion anyway.

774
00:50:15,096 --> 00:50:16,681
Should we go to work
holding hands tomorrow?

775
00:50:16,764 --> 00:50:18,182
Oh, well…

776
00:50:18,266 --> 00:50:20,101
You'll have to go to work alone tomorrow.

777
00:50:20,810 --> 00:50:22,937
-How come?
-I'm taking a day off tomorrow.

778
00:50:23,020 --> 00:50:24,188
Why, all of a sudden?

779
00:50:24,272 --> 00:50:26,190
It's my father's birthday,
so I'm visiting him.

780
00:50:26,274 --> 00:50:28,901
I haven't celebrated his birthday
since my mother passed away.

781
00:50:29,610 --> 00:50:32,029
I'll miss you, but I understand.

782
00:50:32,113 --> 00:50:33,156
Have a safe trip.

783
00:50:35,867 --> 00:50:36,701
Ms. Ji-yoon.

784
00:50:36,784 --> 00:50:37,910
Yes?

785
00:50:37,994 --> 00:50:39,829
Can you promise me something?

786
00:50:41,414 --> 00:50:44,876
Promise you'll make the best choice
for yourself, no matter what.

787
00:50:51,507 --> 00:50:52,884
Yes, I promise.

788
00:51:00,141 --> 00:51:02,518
No-ah, should we go on a trip
when it's spring?

789
00:51:04,479 --> 00:51:06,105
How about we go right now?

790
00:51:06,189 --> 00:51:07,106
Now?

791
00:51:07,857 --> 00:51:08,775
Yeah.

792
00:51:08,858 --> 00:51:10,735
If we put it off, we might never go.

793
00:51:11,527 --> 00:51:13,196
What's wrong? That's not like you.

794
00:51:15,531 --> 00:51:16,449
Jae-in.

795
00:51:17,492 --> 00:51:18,785
I'm going to Senegal.

796
00:51:19,577 --> 00:51:20,703
Senegal?

797
00:51:20,787 --> 00:51:21,704
What for?

798
00:51:23,372 --> 00:51:24,707
My company's sending me.

799
00:51:25,750 --> 00:51:27,376
So it's a business trip?

800
00:51:27,460 --> 00:51:28,461
For how long?

801
00:51:30,421 --> 00:51:31,422
Two years.

802
00:51:39,555 --> 00:51:40,807
Can't you tell them no?

803
00:51:42,391 --> 00:51:43,935
I applied for it myself.

804
00:51:50,525 --> 00:51:52,068
I thought it over so much,

805
00:51:52,151 --> 00:51:53,694
and it was only because of you.

806
00:51:54,278 --> 00:51:55,613
We've just started dating.

807
00:51:56,280 --> 00:51:58,574
If you suddenly leave
for somewhere that far…

808
00:52:01,911 --> 00:52:03,162
Are you breaking up with me?

809
00:52:03,955 --> 00:52:05,832
No, I don't want to break up with you.

810
00:52:07,041 --> 00:52:08,042
But…

811
00:52:09,377 --> 00:52:11,963
I found ambition
for the first time since I started my job.

812
00:52:13,381 --> 00:52:15,925
I want to be recognized more
and climb higher.

813
00:52:16,509 --> 00:52:18,219
But if I stay like this, I'll be stuck

814
00:52:18,302 --> 00:52:20,054
as a Sr. Associate
while everyone gets promoted.

815
00:52:21,472 --> 00:52:22,348
Jae-in.

816
00:52:23,140 --> 00:52:26,519
I'm absolutely sure that going to Senegal
will change everything.

817
00:52:27,436 --> 00:52:29,230
Myself, and my status.

818
00:52:35,945 --> 00:52:37,446
Did you consider me in that choice?

819
00:52:39,448 --> 00:52:40,324
Because it's you.

820
00:52:41,409 --> 00:52:43,661
You're the reason
I got the courage to do this.

821
00:52:44,579 --> 00:52:46,080
The old me before meeting you

822
00:52:46,831 --> 00:52:48,040
wouldn't have dared to do it.

823
00:52:52,378 --> 00:52:53,296
It's just…

824
00:52:55,047 --> 00:52:57,091
before being Lee Jae-in's girlfriend,

825
00:52:58,676 --> 00:53:00,011
I want to be Yoon No-ah first.

826
00:53:09,604 --> 00:53:10,605
I understand.

827
00:53:11,480 --> 00:53:12,481
Do what you want.

828
00:53:16,152 --> 00:53:17,111
But as for me…

829
00:53:20,323 --> 00:53:21,282
I can't do this.

830
00:53:48,392 --> 00:53:49,727
No.

831
00:54:06,035 --> 00:54:07,078
I can't lose you.

832
00:54:08,329 --> 00:54:10,957
I know how incredibly selfish
I'm being right now.

833
00:54:11,040 --> 00:54:11,999
But still…

834
00:54:13,584 --> 00:54:15,336
Can we please stay together?

835
00:54:31,519 --> 00:54:32,436
Jae-in!

836
00:54:34,063 --> 00:54:34,981
Lee Jae-in!

837
00:55:00,089 --> 00:55:01,298
Still haven't heard from him?

838
00:55:01,382 --> 00:55:02,299
No.

839
00:55:03,718 --> 00:55:05,177
I should've said it better.

840
00:55:05,928 --> 00:55:07,555
I don't think I explained it right.

841
00:55:08,556 --> 00:55:10,641
He probably needs time to think too.

842
00:55:10,725 --> 00:55:13,602
It was so sudden,
so his first reaction's bound to be anger.

843
00:55:13,686 --> 00:55:15,438
I would've reacted the same way.

844
00:55:16,522 --> 00:55:19,442
It must feel absurd hearing I'm leaving
when we just got together.

845
00:55:20,026 --> 00:55:22,570
I had no idea you were this brave, No-ah.

846
00:55:22,653 --> 00:55:24,321
First the complaint, now Senegal.

847
00:55:25,031 --> 00:55:26,574
You pulled off two bombshells at once.

848
00:55:26,657 --> 00:55:28,034
This is all your fault.

849
00:55:28,117 --> 00:55:29,535
You totally rubbed off on me.

850
00:55:30,327 --> 00:55:31,370
You're worse than me.

851
00:55:38,753 --> 00:55:40,963
Ji-yoon! Want to grab a drink tonight?

852
00:55:41,047 --> 00:55:43,257
It must be nice getting texts.

853
00:55:44,091 --> 00:55:45,009
It's the Manager, right?

854
00:55:45,676 --> 00:55:46,510
Yes.

855
00:55:49,638 --> 00:55:50,514
I'd love to!

856
00:55:55,394 --> 00:55:56,353
Long time no see.

857
00:55:57,354 --> 00:55:59,065
Well, this is an unexpected duo.

858
00:55:59,690 --> 00:56:01,692
I wanted to grab a drink with Ji-yoon,

859
00:56:01,776 --> 00:56:04,445
but people would gossip
if we stayed near work.

860
00:56:05,154 --> 00:56:06,864
I was the one who suggested this place.

861
00:56:07,490 --> 00:56:08,491
You don't mind, do you?

862
00:56:09,909 --> 00:56:12,161
Hey, I'm grateful for any paying customer.

863
00:56:13,662 --> 00:56:15,039
And I got to see an old friend.

864
00:56:15,623 --> 00:56:17,500
Don't mind me. Go ahead and talk.

865
00:56:21,212 --> 00:56:22,379
Did you have a rough time?

866
00:56:24,632 --> 00:56:25,466
Yes.

867
00:56:26,675 --> 00:56:28,677
I thought the lies would disappear

868
00:56:28,761 --> 00:56:30,471
once I told the truth,

869
00:56:30,971 --> 00:56:33,516
but even bigger lies
ended up blurring the truth.

870
00:56:34,517 --> 00:56:35,601
To be honest,

871
00:56:36,477 --> 00:56:38,020
I was a bit scared.

872
00:56:39,522 --> 00:56:42,441
Still, you hung in there so well.

873
00:56:43,192 --> 00:56:46,612
I heard you even went to HR yourself.

874
00:56:48,155 --> 00:56:48,989
Thank you.

875
00:56:49,573 --> 00:56:51,242
You missed the promotion this time,

876
00:56:52,201 --> 00:56:54,036
but you'll be a Manager soon enough.

877
00:56:55,788 --> 00:56:56,872
Yes.

878
00:56:56,956 --> 00:56:57,873
Prepare yourself.

879
00:56:57,957 --> 00:57:00,334
That's when corporate life really begins.

880
00:57:01,710 --> 00:57:02,795
What's it like?

881
00:57:04,171 --> 00:57:05,673
Wait until you lead a team.

882
00:57:05,756 --> 00:57:09,009
You see right through
your subordinates slacking off

883
00:57:09,593 --> 00:57:11,971
and all the dirty politics
the higher-ups play.

884
00:57:13,472 --> 00:57:15,057
You'll see a side of the company

885
00:57:15,766 --> 00:57:17,393
that you've never seen before.

886
00:57:18,936 --> 00:57:21,730
And on top of that,
if you decide to marry and raise kids,

887
00:57:23,149 --> 00:57:26,110
the glass ceilings you have to break
will look impossibly high.

888
00:57:27,862 --> 00:57:30,614
But you'll do great, Ms Choi.

889
00:57:31,574 --> 00:57:32,449
You know

890
00:57:33,159 --> 00:57:35,202
you're my role model, right?

891
00:57:41,542 --> 00:57:43,961
I'm actually the one
learning a lot from you.

892
00:57:47,173 --> 00:57:49,216
How to work without losing yourself…

893
00:57:53,345 --> 00:57:54,430
and how to love.

894
00:58:00,311 --> 00:58:02,730
I'm counting on you down the road, okay?

895
00:58:02,813 --> 00:58:03,898
Likewise.

896
00:58:05,274 --> 00:58:06,150
You silly.

897
00:58:10,446 --> 00:58:12,364
Man, this feels weird.

898
00:58:25,377 --> 00:58:27,296
You made all of this yourself?

899
00:58:27,379 --> 00:58:28,756
Yes. Why ask the obvious?

900
00:58:28,839 --> 00:58:30,925
All right, then. Let's eat.

901
00:58:42,978 --> 00:58:43,979
It's delicious.

902
00:58:45,231 --> 00:58:46,315
So what brings you here?

903
00:58:47,608 --> 00:58:48,984
It's your birthday.

904
00:58:50,110 --> 00:58:51,654
Birthday? That's nothing special.

905
00:59:11,131 --> 00:59:12,466
Happy birthday.

906
00:59:15,886 --> 00:59:17,972
The sound is probably
just how you remember it.

907
00:59:18,764 --> 00:59:20,307
You should listen to it more often.

908
00:59:20,891 --> 00:59:21,725
It feels like

909
00:59:22,685 --> 00:59:24,353
I dumped a repair job on you.

910
00:59:26,438 --> 00:59:27,856
You're allowed to. I'm your son.

911
00:59:29,984 --> 00:59:33,153
You know, this audio set
belongs by your side.

912
00:59:41,161 --> 00:59:42,746
The soup's getting cold.

913
00:59:43,831 --> 00:59:44,873
Right.

914
01:00:15,946 --> 01:00:18,115
I know he's with his father, but still.

915
01:00:19,033 --> 01:00:21,160
How can he just send one goodnight text

916
01:00:21,243 --> 01:00:22,745
and not even call me once?

917
01:00:23,829 --> 01:00:25,164
It's the weekend, at that.

918
01:00:32,588 --> 01:00:35,341
Wait, is there something I missed?

919
01:00:39,428 --> 01:00:40,346
I'm sorry.

920
01:00:43,766 --> 01:00:44,808
By "rough things,"

921
01:00:45,642 --> 01:00:46,518
do you mean me?

922
01:00:47,603 --> 01:00:48,896
Can you promise me something?

923
01:00:50,189 --> 01:00:53,233
Promise you'll make the best choice
for yourself, no matter what.

924
01:01:10,751 --> 01:01:12,669
Isn't it hard living out here?

925
01:01:13,504 --> 01:01:15,881
Sure, it's less convenient than Seoul.

926
01:01:16,548 --> 01:01:19,009
The grocery stores are far,
and so are the hospitals.

927
01:01:20,302 --> 01:01:23,806
But taking a walk like this
in the sea breeze

928
01:01:24,765 --> 01:01:26,266
completely clears my head.

929
01:01:26,350 --> 01:01:27,351
Time flies as well.

930
01:01:29,353 --> 01:01:30,437
How have you been?

931
01:01:32,981 --> 01:01:33,982
Everything's fine.

932
01:01:34,066 --> 01:01:35,359
Are you sure about that?

933
01:01:35,859 --> 01:01:37,778
Your face is screaming
that you're troubled.

934
01:01:39,154 --> 01:01:41,073
Is everything at work okay?

935
01:01:42,282 --> 01:01:45,369
If I keep at it, I'll get promoted
and even make executive.

936
01:01:46,412 --> 01:01:47,246
But?

937
01:01:47,329 --> 01:01:49,665
I don't think I'll make a good leader.

938
01:01:50,582 --> 01:01:51,625
What do you mean?

939
01:01:53,043 --> 01:01:55,754
A good leader has to be willing
to get their hands dirty

940
01:01:55,838 --> 01:01:58,590
and fight to protect their own people.

941
01:02:01,260 --> 01:02:02,594
I'm not so sure I can do that.

942
01:02:03,262 --> 01:02:04,346
Fair point.

943
01:02:04,430 --> 01:02:07,224
You never had a knack for politics,
just like me.

944
01:02:10,185 --> 01:02:12,146
But that doesn't mean you can't do it.

945
01:02:12,896 --> 01:02:14,731
Office politics comes in different forms.

946
01:02:14,815 --> 01:02:16,650
Some will do this, while others do that.

947
01:02:16,733 --> 01:02:18,569
You just need to do it your own way.

948
01:02:20,988 --> 01:02:24,158
Right. I'm still trying
to figure out what my way is.

949
01:02:29,329 --> 01:02:31,748
It's cold, but it's nice being out.

950
01:02:35,002 --> 01:02:35,878
It is.

951
01:03:11,663 --> 01:03:13,749
What is it? Do you know her?

952
01:03:15,626 --> 01:03:17,085
She's my girlfriend.

953
01:03:24,801 --> 01:03:26,970
I have to go grocery shopping,
so go on home.

954
01:03:28,514 --> 01:03:30,390
We have to feed her dinner
before she goes.

955
01:03:51,578 --> 01:03:52,579
Mr. Kang!

956
01:04:46,341 --> 01:04:47,384
What are you doing here?

957
01:04:48,385 --> 01:04:51,263
I went to your father's place,
but no one was there.

958
01:04:51,346 --> 01:04:54,016
So I was just watching the sea,
waiting for you.

959
01:04:54,975 --> 01:04:56,226
Without even calling me?

960
01:04:57,644 --> 01:05:01,106
I just felt like there was
something going on with you.

961
01:05:11,408 --> 01:05:13,076
I may not know everything,

962
01:05:13,702 --> 01:05:15,412
but I know you're having a hard time.

963
01:05:17,623 --> 01:05:20,500
You keep both the good stuff
and your worries all bottled up,

964
01:05:21,460 --> 01:05:23,170
so you're overthinking by yourself again.

965
01:05:24,880 --> 01:05:26,506
That's why you came all the way here?

966
01:05:28,008 --> 01:05:30,844
I want to be by your side
when you're having a hard time.

967
01:05:36,266 --> 01:05:39,144
I was looking for the answer
in the wrong place.

968
01:05:41,688 --> 01:05:43,732
I was completely lost
searching for the answer,

969
01:05:44,316 --> 01:05:46,318
but it hit me the moment I saw your face.

970
01:05:46,902 --> 01:05:48,153
What answer?

971
01:05:49,029 --> 01:05:50,238
The simplest reason of all.

972
01:05:51,281 --> 01:05:52,282
"Because it's you."

973
01:05:52,991 --> 01:05:53,825
I'm

974
01:05:54,618 --> 01:05:56,036
thinking of quitting my job.

975
01:06:45,836 --> 01:06:48,505
But it feels like a waste to throw away

976
01:06:48,588 --> 01:06:50,340
everything you've worked for.

977
01:06:51,341 --> 01:06:53,009
I want to find out

978
01:06:54,261 --> 01:06:55,220
what I really want to do.

979
01:06:56,012 --> 01:06:57,806
It's not too late to change your mind.

980
01:06:57,889 --> 01:07:00,434
The new hire arrives today.
Can someone be his mentor?

981
01:07:01,226 --> 01:07:02,686
I'll do it.

982
01:07:02,769 --> 01:07:04,563
You're too handsome to work
at an electronics company.

983
01:07:05,355 --> 01:07:07,190
No-ah. Let's get back together.

984
01:07:07,774 --> 01:07:09,818
I know exactly how selfish I'm being.

985
01:07:09,901 --> 01:07:11,528
But I really don't want
to give up on either.

986
01:07:12,028 --> 01:07:12,946
He's…

987
01:07:13,697 --> 01:07:15,949
How can you trust someone
who gives up that easily?

988
01:07:17,075 --> 01:07:19,077
Tomorrow will be my last day at work.

989
01:07:25,751 --> 01:07:27,753
Subtitle: Yenny Kang
